# Module 39 – Advanced Chatbot AI & Knowledge Intelligence

This module upgrades the HI-TECH College chatbot from basic keyword matching to a controlled Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system.

The central rule is that the chatbot must answer college-specific questions using approved institutional knowledge. If it cannot find sufficiently relevant information, it should say so and offer a support request rather than inventing admission requirements, fee amounts, examination dates or college policies.

This implementation adds:

1. Semantic search using text embeddings.
2. RAG responses with references to approved articles.
3. Relevance and confidence thresholds.
4. English and Kiswahili response instructions.
5. Visitor feedback on chatbot answers.
6. Administrator controls for AI configuration.
7. A fallback path when the AI provider is unavailable.

Architecture: React/Vite website → Express chatbot API → approved knowledge retrieval → AI provider → answer with article references. The AI provider remains server-side; no API key is exposed to the browser.

